Description: Cbench HPC benchmarking framework — Python toolchain
 Cbench is a framework for building, running, and parsing HPC benchmarks
 across Linux parallel compute clusters. The Python toolchain (v2.0)
 provides a cbench CLI covering the full benchmark lifecycle:
 .
  * Build benchmark software (stream, HPL, IMB, OSU, IOR, NPB, and more)
  * Generate and submit batch job scripts (SLURM, PBS, LSF, local)
  * Parse benchmark output into structured results (SQLite + JSON)
  * Single-node benchmarking suite (SNB) with direct binary invocation
  * Web dashboard with Prometheus metrics endpoint (optional, needs flask)
